# Ghostty Configuration
#
# KEEP THIS FILE SMALL — see docs/terminal-agnostic-config.md
#
# Everything configured here stops existing the moment another terminal is used
# (Kitty, WezTerm, iTerm2, VS Code's terminal, an SSH session from a borrowed
# machine). Behaviour belongs in tmux or the shell, which are portable; this file
# is for rendering, OS/window integration, and forwarding keys macOS swallows.
#
# The super+<key> block below is exactly that forwarding: it only turns cmd into a
# control code so tmux/the shell can act on it. Do NOT add bindings that implement
# behaviour here (splits, tab switching, resizing) — that behaviour then has to be
# rewritten for every other terminal, forever.

